  "researchNote": "No published Oregon Military Department regulation or statute enumerating the Oregon National Guard state awards program could be located (Oregon Revised Statutes chapter 396, the state's general military affairs chapter, contains no decorations/medals provisions, and the OMD/ONG public site has no awards page). Award names below come from the unsourced Oregon section of Wikipedia's 'List of decorations awarded by the United States National Guard' cross-checked against USA Military Medals (usamm.com) current product listings, which independently confirm 7 of the 10 names as real, currently-sold ribbons (Recruiting, Faithful Service, Superior Soldier, Emergency Service, Commendation Medal, Superior Unit, Exceptional Service). The Oregon Distinguished Service Medal, Meritorious Service Medal, and 30-Year Faithful Service Medal appear only in the Wikipedia list with no USAMM or official corroboration found. None of these two leads constitutes a .mil/.gov/regulation source per the sourcing bar, so the file and every entry are flagged needs-source and no precedence order is asserted. This file supersedes the one-off inline 'Oregon National Guard Faithful Service Ribbon' entry added directly to src/utils/ribbonRackData.js for a specific user's document (a later consolidation pass should retire that inline entry in favor of the 'oregon_national_guard_faithful_service_ribbon' entry here).",
